      "number": 104,
      "title": "Research: Juno control recovery and metadata-qualified nightside pilot",
      "head": "research/juno-uvs-impact-control",
      "sha": "fb0b592b17341fd98c3d560612144c3a7fe6c310",
      "body": "Independent solar-system investigation with executable real-data results:\n\n1. Recovered the published April 10, 2020 control from 112,242 photons.\n2. Prospectively ran a first-500,000-row PJ74 pilot. Its naive triggers fail dayside/scan and telemetry-overflow checks; no events claimed.\n3. Screened housekeeping in all five remaining PJ74 products before photon selection. Selected a 20-second normal-mask, overflow-clear interval and verified nightside geometry. Analyzed 9,787 photons, including 3,016 on-disc nightside photons and 404 longwave photons. Zero fixed-threshold triggers; 20 locally conditioned diagnostic trials also zero. Executed mask, acquisition-tag, housekeeping and ancillary STIM-coordinate checks.\n\nNo new impact, calibrated false-alarm probability, completeness or rate is claimed. Negative pilot results and exact limits are preserved alongside byte hashes and replay scripts. Draft remains open for scientific follow-through. No Chromium tests or CI changes."
    },
