      "number": 102,
      "title": "research: new SPHEREx moving-object spectral search and SWAN validation",
      "head": "research/spherex-dr1-solar-system-20261116",
      "sha": "572f587823ad4a2beda8404cc71f323416da5f94",
      "body": "## Scope\nNew solar-system instrument lane, not expansion of existing results. No discovery claim. Main is untouched.\n\n## Actual work\n- 29P known positive control: 90 selected images, 82 retrieved.\n- Independent targets Echeclus, Wierzchos and SWAN, with negative/inconclusive outcomes preserved.\n- SWAN complete D5 screen: 57 records, 56 retrieved, one HTTP failure. Target-centered spectral excess repeats on December 22/25 and held-out January 2.\n- Official spectral-response calibration, aperture/background tests, ePSF morphology, AllWISE contamination checks and midpoint consistency.\n- The frozen empirical shape fails held-out transfer under formal noise. Molecular identity and composition are not established.\n\n## Review entry\nRead `results/spherex-dr1-moving-spectra/FINAL_STATUS.md`, then `EMPIRICAL_FIT_REPORT.md` and `RESPONSE_VALIDATION.md`. Manifests, source URLs/hashes and successful/failed measurements are included. Calibration retrieval route and hashes are preserved without committing the 436 MB archive.\n\n## Validation\nFour focused unit tests pass; scientific scripts compile. No browser suite or whole-repository CI run. Draft research checkpoint, not a publication-ready discovery."
    }
